ot going to he's not going to  erase  what happened to me all the damage that  these schools did to me it's not going  to erase it it's still here with me  there are members of the community who  will make the trek to quebec city for  the visit but there may not be any  residential school survivors i'm  representing the mall council gonowagi  arnold boye is a member of the band  council he'll be attending his parents  are survivors and he's trying to get  them to go with him but other survivors  have decided the trip would be too long  and difficult at their age so they  backed out unfortunately but their  you know their families will be attended  now there are those who don't think  other members of the community should be  going or that the pope should be coming  they don't want an apology they say as  much as a confession and changes  show me what you're gonna do  show me how you're gonna help us make a  move don't come here and say oh  i'm sorry bless you my child you know  what that does nothing for me  the local school named after gonowagi's  saint was once a residential day school  run by the catholic church that is  something that has changed it's now run  by the community and teaches children  to embrace their mohawk heritage  mike armstrong global news montreal  next a childhood dream comes full circle  a vancouver man fulfills his career wish  more than 150 000 people flooded the  streets of berlin today for one of the  world's largest pride parades it's  christopher street day in germany which  commemorates the riots that broke out in  new york in 1969  after police raided a gay bar  it has been celebrated in germany since  1979. the theme for this year's parade  is united in love  the vancouver police department  introduced its newest team member in a  unique way our camera crew captured the  surprise announcement this week which  was 13 years in the making catherine  ercart explains  it was 2009 when we told you about amman  joanna who used to be a lit